{"full":"hf:Marriam-Fatima/rag-from-scratch","spaceId":"Marriam-Fatima/rag-from-scratch","name":"RAG From Scratch","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":3,"created":"2026-08-23T09:29:32.000Z","updated":"2026-08-23T10:35:28.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://marriam-fatima-rag-from-scratch.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Marriam-Fatima/rag-from-scratch","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:43:58.041Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:43:58.041Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:43:58.041Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔍","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chatbot that answers questions using your own documents instead of the model's memory — with the retrieval core (chunking, embeddings, vector search) implemented from scratch rather than wired to an external vector database or embeddings API.","Most RAG tutorials call a hosted embeddings API and a managed vector DB, which hides exactly the part that makes RAG work: turning text into comparable vectors and searching them efficiently. Implementing TF-IDF and cosine similarity directly makes the tradeoffs (vocabulary size, why normalization matters, why chunk overlap matters) visible and swappable — the same fit/embed interface can later be pointed at a real sentence-transformer or embeddings API without touching the rest of the pipeline."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Marriam-Fatima/rag-from-scratch/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8272db65864ab8ca3a020ba07d645f06a019a10a84911379a1d43cf41943534f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T20:59:31.496Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:43:58.078Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) chatbot t